    "preamble": "Harishankar Rampravesh Singh vs State Of Maharashtra on 10 April, 2024 Author: N. R. Borkar Bench: Prakash D. Naik, N. R. Borkar 17 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Criminal Writ Petition (St) No. 3989 Of 2024 Harishankar Rampravesh Singh ...Pet Versus State Of Maharashtra ...Res With Criminal Writ Petition (St) No. 982 Of 2024 Chhotu Ramkumar Singh ...Pet Versus State Of Maharashtra ...Res With Criminal Writ Petition (St) No. 983 Of 2024 Vikas Umakant Chaudhary ...Pet Versus State Of Maharashtra And Anr.. ...Res With Criminal Writ Petition (St) No. 992 Of 2024 Chandan Umakant Chaudhary ...Pet Versus State Of Maharashtra ...Res With Criminal Writ Petition (St) No. 1453 Of 2024 Faisal Ainul Haque Siddiqui ...Pet Versus State Of Maharashtra ... Res Digitally signed Harishankar Rampravesh Singh vs State Of Maharashtra on 10 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/129479712/ 1 WITH by SUNNY SUNNY ANKUSHRAO ANKUSHRAO THOTE THOTE Date: CRIMINAL WRIT PETITION (ST) NO. 1472 OF 2024 2024.04.15 19:41:16 +0530 Mohammad Ibrahim Shaikh ...Pet Versus State Of Maharashtra ... Res SUNNY THOTE 1 of 3 ::: Uploaded on - 15/04/2024 ::: Downloaded 17-WP(ST)-3989-2024.doc WITH CRIMINAL WRIT PETITION (ST) NO. 326 OF 2024 WITH CRIMINAL WRIT PETITION (ST) NO. 325 OF 2024 Ramesh Shamnarayan Maurya ...Petitioner Versus State Of Maharashtra ...Respondent WITH CRIMINAL WRIT PETITION (ST) NO. 2747 OF 2024 Ramvilas @ Rambilash Banarasi Yadav And Anr. ...Petitioners Versus State Of Maharashtra And Anr. ...Respondents .... Mr. Tushar Sonawane, Advocate for the Petitioners. Ms. M.M. Deshmukh, APP for Respondent - State. Mr. Mahendra Patil, API, DCB-CID, Unit-9, Bandra(W), Mumbai. PSI, Takmoye, Pant Nagar Police Station. Mr. Swapnil B., Kashimire Police Station. API, R.C. Powar, Manor Police Station, Palghar in WP/2747/2024. Mr. Sajay Reday, PSI, Crime Branch, Navi Mumbai Police Station in WP/326/2024 .... Harishankar Rampravesh Singh vs State Of Maharashtra on 10 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/129479712/ 2 CORAM : PRAKASH D. NAIK, & N. R. BORKAR, JJ. DATE : 10th APRIL, 2024. P.C.: 1.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "In all these matters the Petitioners have raised the issue of applicability of Section 328 of Indian Penal Code and non maintainability of simultaneous proceedings for the offences under SUNNY THOTE 2 of 3 17-WP(ST)-3989-2024.doc the Indian Penal Code and Food Safety and Standards Act. 2. Learned Counsel for the Petitioners has relied upon the decision of Apex Court in the case of Ram Nath V/s. State of Uttar Pradesh and Others, 2024 SCC OnLine SC 177. 3."
